WEBVTT

00:00:06.152 --> 00:00:10.823
A NETFLIX ORIGINAL ANIME FILM

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:21.083
<i>Apartments with fresh ivy</i>

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:23.252
<i>We're in number 305</i>

00:00:24.253 --> 00:00:25.463
<i>Far across the sky</i>

00:00:26.047 --> 00:00:27.506
<i>above the green rice paddies</i>

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:29.175
<i>is the dwindling sun</i>

00:00:29.258 --> 00:00:30.092
<i>#HAIKU</i>

00:00:35.806 --> 00:00:36.849
<i>The water strider</i>

00:00:37.558 --> 00:00:39.351
<i>leaves a ripple</i>

00:00:39.435 --> 00:00:40.770
<i>on the water's surface</i>

00:00:44.565 --> 00:00:45.983
<i>Our summer clothes</i>

00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:47.860
<i>match the rice paddies</i>

00:00:47.943 --> 00:00:49.320
<i>in my hometown</i>

00:01:42.414 --> 00:01:44.291
Smile for me!

00:01:47.837 --> 00:01:53.884
FLYINGDOG 10TH ANNIVERSARY PROJECT

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:07.523
WORDS BUBBLE UP LIKE SODA POP

00:02:26.917 --> 00:02:31.839
ODA NOUVELLE MALL

00:02:31.922 --> 00:02:33.382
THERE ARE SO MANY

00:02:33.465 --> 00:02:35.342
LOOKING UP ABOVE

00:02:35.426 --> 00:02:36.886
SUMMER HAS ARRIVED

00:02:36.969 --> 00:02:40.389
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

00:02:48.898 --> 00:02:51.275
A FROG JUMPS
WATER DROPLETS GLISTEN

00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:53.652
EVERY COLOR
ALL INTERTWINED

00:03:19.762 --> 00:03:23.641
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

00:03:35.986 --> 00:03:37.404
Mr. Fujiyama!

00:03:39.782 --> 00:03:40.866
Mr. Fujiyama?

00:03:42.785 --> 00:03:44.787
Mr. Fujiyama!

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:48.874
Oh! Well, if it isn't Cherry Boy!

00:03:48.958 --> 00:03:50.292
Did you find it?

00:03:50.376 --> 00:03:51.669
Nope.

00:03:51.752 --> 00:03:54.630
I see. Then let's go home.

00:03:54.713 --> 00:03:55.589
Mm…

00:03:57.216 --> 00:04:00.469
CHERRY

00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:08.894
SATURDAY, JULY 20

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.490
TAMA DENTAL CLINIC

00:04:21.573 --> 00:04:24.743
-Okay, open up and say "Eee."
-Eee.

00:04:24.827 --> 00:04:26.120
-Open wide.
-Ah.

00:04:26.203 --> 00:04:27.997
-Now close.
-Eee.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.415
Does it feel okay?

00:04:29.498 --> 00:04:30.457
Yes.

00:04:30.541 --> 00:04:31.875
Then we're all done.

00:04:32.418 --> 00:04:34.086
Brushing might be tough,

00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:37.339
so be sure to rinse
with an antiseptic mouthwash.

00:04:37.548 --> 00:04:38.424
Okay.

00:04:39.174 --> 00:04:41.927
All right,
I'll see you at your next check-up.

00:04:42.553 --> 00:04:43.554
Take care.

00:04:43.637 --> 00:04:45.639
TAMA DENTAL CLINIC

00:04:59.361 --> 00:05:00.571
All right!

00:05:01.196 --> 00:05:04.283
SMILE@ORANGESUNSHINE

00:05:07.661 --> 00:05:09.246
<i>Can you hear me, everyone?</i>

00:05:09.913 --> 00:05:12.249
<i>Hey, are you smiling every day?</i>

00:05:12.875 --> 00:05:15.252
<i>We're the sparkling idol sisters.</i>

00:05:15.336 --> 00:05:18.130
<i>I'm Smile, from OrangeSunshine!</i>

00:05:18.213 --> 00:05:20.632
<i>Smile for me!</i>

00:05:22.009 --> 00:05:24.928
<i>Wow, so many likes!</i>

00:05:25.012 --> 00:05:26.805
<i>Thank you, everyone!</i>

00:05:27.348 --> 00:05:29.600
<i>You're commenting too fast.</i>

00:05:30.225 --> 00:05:33.312
<i>I'll show you all the cute things</i>
<i>that I found today.</i>

00:05:33.854 --> 00:05:36.899
<i>If you think they're cute, too,</i>
<i>give me a like.</i>

00:05:37.608 --> 00:05:38.442
<i>By the way…</i>

00:05:41.487 --> 00:05:43.238
<i>I'm at the local mall today.</i>

00:05:46.325 --> 00:05:49.119
<i>It's summer break,</i>
<i>so there are a lot of people.</i>

00:05:53.999 --> 00:05:56.585
<i>Gotta be careful not to bump into anyone.</i>

00:05:56.668 --> 00:05:58.837
<i>Okay, let's all say it together.</i>

00:05:59.338 --> 00:06:01.673
Smile-smile!

00:06:03.342 --> 00:06:04.593
<i>Wow, look at this!</i>

00:06:04.676 --> 00:06:07.096
A small vending machine. So cute.

00:06:07.763 --> 00:06:08.931
A train made out of carts!

00:06:09.556 --> 00:06:10.849
A Hikarun cut-out.

00:06:11.433 --> 00:06:12.810
Daruma! Huh?

00:06:13.685 --> 00:06:14.520
<i>What?</i>

00:06:15.104 --> 00:06:16.814
<i>Come on, daruma are cute.</i>

00:06:21.443 --> 00:06:24.071
It's pretty crowded now, right, Motopuri?

00:06:24.154 --> 00:06:25.697
My name's Shirai.

00:06:26.448 --> 00:06:29.201
It's summer break,
so there are more students.

00:06:29.326 --> 00:06:30.202
Hmm?

00:06:30.285 --> 00:06:32.079
Did it move?

00:06:32.162 --> 00:06:33.205
You mean Hikarun?

00:06:33.288 --> 00:06:35.207
There's no way… What?

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.211
Beaver!

00:06:47.553 --> 00:06:49.805
It's another dud.

00:06:51.056 --> 00:06:53.183
Is the rare Hikarun figure even in there?

00:06:53.267 --> 00:06:54.476
Hey, that's mine!

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.603
Japan.

00:06:58.313 --> 00:07:01.191
A life-sized Hikarun!

00:07:01.817 --> 00:07:02.693
It's all ours.

00:07:02.776 --> 00:07:05.487
You're amazing.

00:07:06.155 --> 00:07:07.865
It's what you wanted, right?

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:11.743
Hey, you took off
with store property again!

00:07:11.827 --> 00:07:14.037
Mess with grownups
and face the consequences!

00:07:15.622 --> 00:07:16.957
I'm sorry.

00:07:31.722 --> 00:07:33.599
I'm borrowing this.

00:07:42.733 --> 00:07:44.485
Now to my <i>base secreta!</i>

00:07:45.527 --> 00:07:47.488
Beaver!

00:07:47.571 --> 00:07:48.447
Motopuri?

00:08:04.588 --> 00:08:05.756
Get out of the way!

00:08:11.428 --> 00:08:14.640
All right, it's time for
the baby-crawl race!

00:08:14.723 --> 00:08:17.601
Get in position. Ready?

00:08:17.684 --> 00:08:19.728
Oh! Wait, hold on!

00:08:19.811 --> 00:08:21.313
We haven't started yet.

00:08:21.396 --> 00:08:22.231
Wait!

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.650
Hey, that was a false start.

00:08:25.234 --> 00:08:27.444
It was a false start!

00:08:28.487 --> 00:08:30.239
"It was a false start."

00:08:30.781 --> 00:08:32.616
"It was a false start."

00:08:33.575 --> 00:08:35.327
HAIKU <i>KIGO</i>
SEASONAL WORD DICTIONARY

00:08:37.996 --> 00:08:38.830
"False…"

00:08:39.665 --> 00:08:40.666
"False…"

00:08:46.672 --> 00:08:49.550
It's a crawling race! How cute.

00:08:54.805 --> 00:08:56.807
Wow, so many people.

00:08:58.684 --> 00:09:00.686
"False start…"

00:09:00.769 --> 00:09:03.188
Nope, it's not listed as a seasonal word.

00:09:10.904 --> 00:09:12.531
Beaver!

00:09:13.615 --> 00:09:14.783
Hey, whoa!

00:09:45.147 --> 00:09:46.565
Braces?

00:10:00.746 --> 00:10:02.748
Beaver!

00:10:04.416 --> 00:10:05.292
Adieu!

00:10:05.375 --> 00:10:07.836
Hold it right there, Beaver!

00:10:09.212 --> 00:10:11.256
"Braces…"

00:10:12.466 --> 00:10:14.843
"Braces…"

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:25.479
Beaver, that punk!

00:10:29.983 --> 00:10:32.444
I'm gonna beat him to a pulp!

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:37.949
DAY SERVICE HIDAMARI

00:10:38.033 --> 00:10:39.951
AGING IS THE EXPLOSION OF LIFE
- FUJIYAMA

00:10:41.953 --> 00:10:43.413
ALWAYS BE LIVELY AND WELL

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.630
We're back.

00:10:51.713 --> 00:10:53.715
Oh, Cherry. Welcome back.

00:10:55.509 --> 00:10:57.386
You too, Fujiyama.

00:10:57.469 --> 00:10:58.804
Mm-hmm.

00:10:58.887 --> 00:11:02.099
Thank you as always, Cherry.

00:11:02.182 --> 00:11:03.475
It's no big deal.

00:11:04.267 --> 00:11:06.520
Fujiyama, did you find it?

00:11:11.983 --> 00:11:13.068
Nope.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:15.862
Is that so?

00:11:18.365 --> 00:11:19.491
Oh, Cherry.

00:11:20.617 --> 00:11:21.785
Not while working.

00:11:21.868 --> 00:11:22.703
Oh!

00:11:24.788 --> 00:11:25.706
Nami.

00:11:25.789 --> 00:11:28.959
What is Fujiyama always looking for?

00:11:29.042 --> 00:11:32.045
He said he's looking for a record.

00:11:32.129 --> 00:11:35.424
A record?
You mean the thing he's always holding?

00:11:35.507 --> 00:11:37.300
Yeah, the record that goes inside.

00:11:37.384 --> 00:11:40.262
He must've forgotten where he put it.

00:11:40.345 --> 00:11:42.556
Would it even be in this mall?

00:11:42.639 --> 00:11:43.473
Who knows?

00:11:44.725 --> 00:11:45.934
<i>Like your emotions</i>

00:11:46.017 --> 00:11:48.854
<i>Rise above the sea, young one</i>

00:11:48.937 --> 00:11:50.355
You're too loud.

00:11:50.439 --> 00:11:54.443
<i>Like your emotions</i>
<i>Rise above the sea, young one</i>

00:11:54.526 --> 00:11:56.319
Hmm, that's…

00:11:57.028 --> 00:11:59.239
Settsu. Yukihiko Settsu.

00:11:59.322 --> 00:12:00.490
Uh-huh.

00:12:00.574 --> 00:12:03.702
Settsu's haikus have
an unusual rhythm to them.

00:12:03.785 --> 00:12:06.997
Adding sound to an image…

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.123
It is indeed…

00:12:08.623 --> 00:12:10.167
Sound to an image?

00:12:12.544 --> 00:12:15.714
Um, Mr. Fujiyama, could you
keep your voice down next time…

00:12:15.797 --> 00:12:16.965
What did you say?

00:12:17.466 --> 00:12:19.384
-Your voice…
-What?

00:12:20.719 --> 00:12:22.053
It's nothing.

00:12:22.137 --> 00:12:23.430
Hey, Cherry!

00:12:23.513 --> 00:12:24.848
Where's that punk, Beaver?

00:12:24.931 --> 00:12:25.766
Oh!

00:12:25.849 --> 00:12:27.684
Toughboy's here.

00:12:27.768 --> 00:12:29.352
Oh, Akiko!

00:12:29.936 --> 00:12:31.188
Good to see you.

00:12:31.772 --> 00:12:35.609
Mr. Fujiyama,
your grandson is here to pick you up.

00:12:37.611 --> 00:12:38.904
Akiko…

00:12:40.906 --> 00:12:43.533
Right! Where's that punk, Beaver?

00:12:43.617 --> 00:12:44.534
I don't know.

00:12:44.618 --> 00:12:47.454
He drew graffiti on my car again.

00:12:47.537 --> 00:12:48.747
"Hear comes…?"

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:50.957
Freaking Cherry Boy!

00:12:51.041 --> 00:12:53.335
Mess with me and I'll beat you up!

00:12:53.418 --> 00:12:55.086
I'm not messing with you.

00:12:57.464 --> 00:12:59.466
DAY SERVICE HIMADAMARI

00:13:00.383 --> 00:13:01.968
If you see him,

00:13:02.052 --> 00:13:04.221
tell him I'll beat him to a pulp.

00:13:07.766 --> 00:13:11.019
Cherry, your shift is almost up for today.

00:13:11.102 --> 00:13:12.270
Good work.

00:13:17.651 --> 00:13:18.902
Have a good day.

00:13:19.444 --> 00:13:21.154
Have a good day.

00:13:21.238 --> 00:13:22.656
BLUE-AND-WHITE FLYCATCHER

00:13:22.739 --> 00:13:25.575
STANDING TALL IN AQUAMARINE BLUE

00:13:25.659 --> 00:13:26.660
Beaver, that guy…

00:13:50.517 --> 00:13:54.062
He said "braces"!

00:13:54.145 --> 00:13:56.481
Oh! My mask is gone!

00:14:09.744 --> 00:14:11.037
SEASONAL <i>KIGO</i> DICTIONARY

00:14:12.789 --> 00:14:14.749
Huh? Whose phone is this?

00:14:18.837 --> 00:14:20.255
The guy with the headphones…

00:14:24.426 --> 00:14:26.761
Is this a dictionary?

00:14:29.264 --> 00:14:32.642
Wait, my phone! What do I do?

00:15:04.633 --> 00:15:06.760
Hey, Japan.

00:15:06.843 --> 00:15:08.511
It's me, Hikarun.

00:15:08.595 --> 00:15:10.889
I'm so glad we're finally meeting!

00:15:10.972 --> 00:15:13.433
I was so lone-- Huh?

00:15:17.812 --> 00:15:19.147
You're the worst.

00:15:21.024 --> 00:15:22.484
The deal's off.

00:15:22.567 --> 00:15:23.985
Hey, don't mess with me!

00:15:24.069 --> 00:15:26.363
You tore her head off, idiot!

00:15:26.446 --> 00:15:27.864
I have her body, too!

00:15:27.948 --> 00:15:30.075
That's not the problem here!

00:15:30.992 --> 00:15:34.245
Hikarun!

00:15:40.794 --> 00:15:43.171
Oh, Cherry. Sorry about earlier.

00:15:43.672 --> 00:15:44.547
It's fine.

00:15:45.131 --> 00:15:48.426
Motopuri was so persistent.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.553
Oh, Toughboy was looking for you.

00:15:51.221 --> 00:15:55.767
"Here comes Toughboy!"
I wrote it on his car.

00:15:55.850 --> 00:15:57.519
-"Hear."
-Huh?

00:15:58.103 --> 00:15:59.938
You wrote "hear," not "here."

00:16:00.438 --> 00:16:02.857
You wrote "Hear comes Toughboy."

00:16:02.941 --> 00:16:04.734
But I wrote "here"!

00:16:08.321 --> 00:16:09.239
I'm home!

00:16:09.322 --> 00:16:10.782
Welcome home.

00:16:11.282 --> 00:16:13.493
Yuki, don't run in the house!

00:16:13.576 --> 00:16:14.577
Okay!

00:16:18.039 --> 00:16:19.874
Mari, help me!

00:16:20.834 --> 00:16:22.752
Yuki, keep it down.

00:16:22.836 --> 00:16:24.963
I have a practice exam tomorrow.

00:16:25.046 --> 00:16:26.923
Huh? Where's Mari?

00:16:27.007 --> 00:16:27.966
What?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:29.426
What's up?

00:16:30.427 --> 00:16:31.678
Mari!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:36.641
My phone! Can you look up where it is?

00:16:36.725 --> 00:16:39.310
-You're holding it.
-This isn't mine!

00:16:40.353 --> 00:16:41.563
Huh?

00:16:41.646 --> 00:16:43.732
THERE ARE SO MANY
LOOKING DOWN BELOW

00:16:43.815 --> 00:16:45.358
SUMMER HAS ARRIVED

00:16:46.568 --> 00:16:48.486
I'm getting pretty good.

00:16:48.570 --> 00:16:50.780
Aren't these all Cherry's haikus?

00:16:50.864 --> 00:16:51.698
That's right.

00:16:51.781 --> 00:16:53.575
So squiggly. I can't read it.

00:16:53.658 --> 00:16:55.326
It's graffiti, idiot.

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:58.329
I'm using Cherry's haikus
to study Japanese.

00:16:58.413 --> 00:17:00.999
-You speak it just fine.
-I can't write.

00:17:01.082 --> 00:17:03.793
And my Dad can only write in Spanish.

00:17:05.045 --> 00:17:07.589
You're tagging my haikus
all over the mall.

00:17:07.672 --> 00:17:09.674
And at the apartment building.

00:17:09.758 --> 00:17:11.843
Knock it off. It's embarrassing.

00:17:11.926 --> 00:17:12.802
Why?

00:17:12.886 --> 00:17:14.721
Your rhymes are so cool.

00:17:15.221 --> 00:17:17.140
They're haikus, not rhymes.

00:17:30.820 --> 00:17:32.363
Evening…

00:17:33.448 --> 00:17:35.033
The evening sunset…

00:17:35.158 --> 00:17:36.826
What? Is this a new haiku?

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:37.869
It's nothing.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.289
"The evening sun"… Huh?

00:17:41.956 --> 00:17:44.584
Whose phone is this?

00:17:47.003 --> 00:17:48.254
Braces…

00:17:51.049 --> 00:17:52.801
Without your phone, you'll die.

00:17:52.884 --> 00:17:54.761
-I'm gonna die.
-You won't die.

00:17:54.844 --> 00:17:57.514
-Anyone would die without their phone.
-I would.

00:17:57.597 --> 00:18:00.350
I need it back today or I'll die.

00:18:00.433 --> 00:18:01.643
-Found it!
-Really?

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:05.563
-Is that the mall?
-It is.

00:18:05.647 --> 00:18:06.689
You found it?

00:18:06.773 --> 00:18:09.150
-It's at the mall. Be right back.
-Good luck!

00:18:09.234 --> 00:18:11.277
Why don't you try calling first?

00:18:11.361 --> 00:18:13.196
I told you, it's at the mall!

00:18:13.947 --> 00:18:16.116
If you call, someone might pick up.

00:18:17.408 --> 00:18:18.701
You grabbed the wrong phone?

00:18:18.785 --> 00:18:20.578
When we ran into each other.

00:18:20.662 --> 00:18:22.330
Huh? Was it my fault?

00:18:22.413 --> 00:18:23.998
Oh, someone's calling.

00:18:24.082 --> 00:18:26.251
Wait, what should I do?

00:18:26.334 --> 00:18:27.544
Just pick up.

00:18:27.627 --> 00:18:29.254
I can't…

00:18:29.337 --> 00:18:31.047
-Hey!
-Here.

00:18:31.131 --> 00:18:32.632
<i>Hello?</i>

00:18:33.216 --> 00:18:34.342
<i>Anyone there?</i>

00:18:34.425 --> 00:18:36.469
<i>Um, can you hear me?</i>

00:18:37.929 --> 00:18:39.180
Hello?

00:18:39.722 --> 00:18:41.599
They picked up, but they won't talk.

00:18:42.183 --> 00:18:43.768
Say something already.

00:18:44.477 --> 00:18:45.395
No, I can't.

00:18:46.354 --> 00:18:48.064
Ah, I need a mask!

00:18:48.148 --> 00:18:50.650
Geez, why does he want a video call?

00:18:53.403 --> 00:18:54.863
Yeah, it's him.

00:18:54.946 --> 00:18:57.157
Um, that phone you have is--

00:18:57.240 --> 00:18:59.242
Smile for me!

00:18:59.325 --> 00:19:00.702
Oh, she hung up.

00:19:00.785 --> 00:19:02.120
What was that just now?

00:19:02.203 --> 00:19:03.163
One of our viewers?

00:19:03.246 --> 00:19:05.290
Juri, you ended the call.

00:19:05.373 --> 00:19:07.584
Sorry, he was just so intense.

00:19:07.667 --> 00:19:10.587
Wasn't that Smile just now? No way!

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:12.005
Who's Smile?

00:19:12.088 --> 00:19:14.549
She's a famous
high-school Curiosity influencer.

00:19:14.632 --> 00:19:16.551
-Cherry, do you know her?
-No.

00:19:16.634 --> 00:19:19.679
You idiot, she has
so many views on CurioLive!

00:19:19.762 --> 00:19:21.264
It's over a million views.

00:19:21.764 --> 00:19:22.932
Answer it!

00:19:23.016 --> 00:19:24.309
No, I can't.

00:19:24.392 --> 00:19:25.226
Hey!

00:19:26.686 --> 00:19:28.438
Sorry, that wasn't directed at you.

00:19:29.314 --> 00:19:30.398
Um…

00:19:31.274 --> 00:19:32.734
I'm sorry.

00:19:35.528 --> 00:19:37.947
WEDNESDAY, JULY 24

00:19:39.616 --> 00:19:42.118
Isn't this great? You got your phone back.

00:19:42.202 --> 00:19:43.411
I'm so glad.

00:19:43.494 --> 00:19:45.955
I was so worried about it.

00:19:46.039 --> 00:19:47.790
You got out of it alive.

00:19:47.874 --> 00:19:48.750
Yeah.

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:02.138
-Why are you eating like that?
-Is it a trend?

00:20:02.222 --> 00:20:03.431
Leave me alone.

00:20:03.514 --> 00:20:05.433
TODAY'S SCHEDULE:

00:20:05.516 --> 00:20:08.228
LOOKING FOR POETRY INSPIRATION
AT MALL WITH MS. MIYUKI

00:20:08.311 --> 00:20:09.687
Have fun.

00:20:09.771 --> 00:20:12.065
Thanks, Cherry and Ms. Miyuki.

00:20:12.148 --> 00:20:14.400
All right, let's head out.

00:20:17.946 --> 00:20:19.906
Let's clean while they're away.

00:20:19.989 --> 00:20:20.823
Okay.

00:20:22.825 --> 00:20:23.826
Boss, what's wrong?

00:20:24.577 --> 00:20:26.579
What will we do after Obon break?

00:20:27.330 --> 00:20:29.332
Are the shifts not filling up?

00:20:30.041 --> 00:20:31.709
We need to find a new part-timer.

00:20:31.793 --> 00:20:32.627
KOUICHI SAKURA

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:35.046
We'll have to get serious
about finding someone.

00:20:35.129 --> 00:20:36.047
Yes.

00:20:38.174 --> 00:20:41.636
GO! SUMMER BARGAIN

00:20:41.719 --> 00:20:44.597
Oh, look, we can use that.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.439
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

00:20:54.607 --> 00:20:56.401
Is being seen with them that bad?

00:20:56.484 --> 00:20:58.319
Yeah, they're gross.

00:20:58.403 --> 00:21:01.698
Yuki, you'll be a mecha girl.
It's totally in! You'll be popular.

00:21:01.781 --> 00:21:02.782
No way.

00:21:02.865 --> 00:21:03.741
I mean…

00:21:04.575 --> 00:21:08.496
<i>Your buck teeth were always</i>
<i>your best feature since you were young.</i>

00:21:08.579 --> 00:21:09.664
<i>Yeah, but…</i>

00:21:09.747 --> 00:21:11.541
<i>Yeah, it's cute!</i>

00:21:11.624 --> 00:21:13.251
<i>Our viewers loved it, too.</i>

00:21:13.334 --> 00:21:14.627
<i>The beaver smile.</i>

00:21:14.711 --> 00:21:16.379
<i>I'm not a beaver.</i>

00:21:17.046 --> 00:21:19.465
You liked it too, didn't you?

00:21:20.675 --> 00:21:21.968
I did, but…

00:21:22.844 --> 00:21:23.886
It's…

00:21:59.756 --> 00:22:01.174
DISPOSABLE FACE MASKS

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:18.775
It's not cute.

00:22:19.525 --> 00:22:21.319
What a teenager.

00:22:21.402 --> 00:22:23.446
-Do you hate your braces, too?
-I do.

00:22:23.529 --> 00:22:26.074
But they're cute, they're totally mecha.

00:22:26.157 --> 00:22:27.492
Mari.

00:22:27.575 --> 00:22:31.162
Well, I do understand
waking up one morning

00:22:31.245 --> 00:22:32.955
and hating how you look.

00:22:33.039 --> 00:22:34.332
That's happened to you?

00:22:34.415 --> 00:22:36.292
Yeah, it has.

00:22:38.711 --> 00:22:39.879
It's that guy!

00:22:39.962 --> 00:22:41.214
From the video call.

00:22:48.721 --> 00:22:50.431
He's into more mature types?

00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:54.602
<i>He looked unsociable,</i>
<i>but he has a girlfriend.</i>

00:22:54.685 --> 00:22:57.021
-Siblings, maybe?
<i>-They don't look related.</i>

00:23:08.741 --> 00:23:11.661
THE SHOPPING MALL

00:23:11.744 --> 00:23:15.123
MELTS IN THE EVENING SUN

00:23:15.206 --> 00:23:17.250
#HAIKU

00:23:29.637 --> 00:23:32.306
MARIA LIKED YOUR COMMENT

00:23:34.142 --> 00:23:38.104
Let's present the haikus we wrote today.

00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:43.860
Write your poem with your calligraphy pen
on the paper strips I gave you.

00:23:46.571 --> 00:23:49.073
She kind of looks like a teacher.

00:23:49.157 --> 00:23:50.408
What are they doing?

00:23:51.617 --> 00:23:53.870
Okay, once you're done,

00:23:53.953 --> 00:23:55.538
I'll collect it from you.

00:23:57.081 --> 00:24:01.252
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

00:24:15.475 --> 00:24:16.392
All right.

00:24:16.476 --> 00:24:19.729
I will now recite the poems for you all.

00:24:21.355 --> 00:24:23.483
MALL MANNEQUINS WEAR <i>YUKATA</i> TOO
- SASAKI

00:24:24.233 --> 00:24:28.905
<i>"Mall mannequins wear yukata, too."</i>

00:24:29.572 --> 00:24:33.701
<i>"Mall mannequins wear yukata, too."</i>

00:24:34.619 --> 00:24:38.122
By seeing the store mannequins in <i>yukata,</i>

00:24:38.206 --> 00:24:41.459
you can tell that it's summer now.

00:24:41.542 --> 00:24:43.711
You can feel the season.

00:24:44.462 --> 00:24:47.215
This was written by Mr. Sasaki.

00:24:48.966 --> 00:24:50.927
Let's look at the next one.

00:24:54.555 --> 00:24:56.182
-Cherry?
-Yes?

00:24:56.933 --> 00:24:59.352
Can you come over here?

00:25:13.574 --> 00:25:15.201
This is my haiku.

00:25:17.203 --> 00:25:19.330
Please recite it for us.

00:25:19.413 --> 00:25:20.706
What!

00:25:20.790 --> 00:25:21.958
Is that a no?

00:25:22.041 --> 00:25:23.876
No, it's just…

00:25:24.877 --> 00:25:30.508
Reading in front of people
is not really my style.

00:25:30.591 --> 00:25:33.302
But everyone wants to hear it.

00:25:39.225 --> 00:25:43.312
Please read it to everyone
with your wonderful voice.

00:26:02.081 --> 00:26:02.999
<i>The…</i>

00:26:09.964 --> 00:26:11.215
<i>The shopping mall</i>

00:26:15.678 --> 00:26:17.430
<i>melts in the evening sun</i>

00:26:17.513 --> 00:26:19.265
What?

00:26:19.348 --> 00:26:22.351
Cherry, say it a bit louder.

00:26:32.778 --> 00:26:34.822
<i>The shopping mall</i>
<i>melts in the evening sun</i>

00:26:43.998 --> 00:26:45.666
THE SHOPPING MALL MELTS…

00:26:51.547 --> 00:26:53.132
Thank you very much.

00:27:00.681 --> 00:27:02.141
Haiku…

00:27:02.975 --> 00:27:04.685
is a written art form.

00:27:08.147 --> 00:27:10.399
It doesn't have to be read aloud.

00:27:13.069 --> 00:27:14.403
That's true.

00:27:14.487 --> 00:27:18.324
But don't you think
some scenes can only be conveyed

00:27:18.407 --> 00:27:19.909
when you read them aloud?

00:27:21.994 --> 00:27:25.247
But it does get across,
even without being read aloud.

00:27:26.999 --> 00:27:28.709
<i>The cicadas can be heard</i>

00:27:28.793 --> 00:27:31.379
<i>even by the girl behind her mask</i>

00:27:32.338 --> 00:27:33.631
<i>The cicadas can be heard</i>

00:27:33.714 --> 00:27:36.509
<i>even by the girl behind her mask</i>

00:27:51.065 --> 00:27:53.651
So you're a year older?

00:27:53.734 --> 00:27:56.112
I… guess I am.

00:27:58.531 --> 00:28:00.908
Now I see why you're named Cherry.

00:28:00.991 --> 00:28:03.411
Your surname, "Sakura,"
means "cherry blossom."

00:28:03.494 --> 00:28:06.580
-Oh, right.
-Cherry is a cute name.

00:28:06.664 --> 00:28:07.832
"Mr. Cherry"?

00:28:09.375 --> 00:28:11.585
Or maybe just "Cherry" sounds better.

00:28:14.922 --> 00:28:16.549
What are you listening to?

00:28:16.632 --> 00:28:18.801
Huh? Well…

00:28:20.845 --> 00:28:22.972
I've always disliked loud sounds.

00:28:23.806 --> 00:28:26.726
-I'm not actually listening to anything.
-What?

00:28:26.809 --> 00:28:30.521
If I do this, I can get by
without people talking to me.

00:28:30.604 --> 00:28:32.606
Oh, that's so smart.

00:28:40.281 --> 00:28:42.074
-A summer cold?
-Huh?

00:28:44.910 --> 00:28:46.662
This is, um…

00:28:46.746 --> 00:28:49.665
Oh, why did you attach a dictionary
to your phone?

00:28:49.749 --> 00:28:52.877
-Hm? Oh, that's a <i>saijiki.</i>
-A <i>"saijiki"?</i>

00:28:54.003 --> 00:28:56.422
It's a dictionary used for writing haikus.

00:28:57.673 --> 00:28:59.675
There is an app version, too,

00:28:59.759 --> 00:29:02.386
but I like having the book more.

00:29:03.179 --> 00:29:05.264
You must like haikus.

00:29:06.140 --> 00:29:09.477
Haikus help me
express things in words better.

00:29:09.560 --> 00:29:10.895
Or something.

00:29:11.771 --> 00:29:13.564
But I'm no good at…

00:29:14.607 --> 00:29:16.233
reading in front of people.

00:29:18.903 --> 00:29:23.073
-I sometimes upload it on Curiosity.
-I get it.

00:29:24.033 --> 00:29:27.453
If it's online,
everyone will look at it more.

00:29:27.536 --> 00:29:29.371
I totally get it.

00:29:33.667 --> 00:29:35.503
FOLLOWING: 84
FOLLOWERS: 4

00:29:36.212 --> 00:29:37.505
JAPAN: FROM PLANET HIKARUN

00:29:37.588 --> 00:29:38.839
MARIA: I LOVE CUTE THINGS!

00:29:38.923 --> 00:29:40.049
HAIKU BOT: POSTS HAIKUS

00:29:40.132 --> 00:29:41.091
FIND FRIENDS

00:29:41.759 --> 00:29:43.677
Nobody reads them.

00:29:45.262 --> 00:29:46.305
Do they come easily?

00:29:47.765 --> 00:29:48.599
The haikus.

00:29:49.225 --> 00:29:50.851
On good days.

00:29:50.935 --> 00:29:53.270
Wow, then try making one.

00:29:53.354 --> 00:29:55.105
What? Right now?

00:29:56.106 --> 00:29:59.693
Sorry, that might've sounded a bit pushy.

00:30:11.872 --> 00:30:13.207
Lights in the summer night…

00:30:30.933 --> 00:30:32.268
<i>Lights in the summer night</i>

00:30:32.768 --> 00:30:35.729
<i>make a false start</i>
<i>in the evening sunset</i>

00:30:42.987 --> 00:30:44.530
<i>Lights in the summer night</i>

00:30:45.531 --> 00:30:48.325
<i>make a false start</i>
<i>in the evening sunset</i>

00:30:51.161 --> 00:30:54.081
What do you mean by
"lights in the summer night"?

00:30:54.957 --> 00:30:56.333
It's about "lights."

00:30:56.417 --> 00:30:58.544
It's a summer <i>kigo,</i> a seasonal word.

00:30:59.128 --> 00:31:00.296
A <i>"kigo"…</i>

00:31:04.967 --> 00:31:08.220
<i>Lights in the summer night</i>
<i>make a false start</i>

00:31:08.304 --> 00:31:09.555
<i>in the evening sunset</i>

00:31:13.350 --> 00:31:14.560
It's so cute!

00:31:20.816 --> 00:31:22.026
Cute?

00:31:22.109 --> 00:31:23.068
Yeah.

00:31:24.737 --> 00:31:25.779
What part of it?

00:31:28.115 --> 00:31:31.535
The "make a false start" part.

00:31:32.453 --> 00:31:33.287
And…

00:31:36.457 --> 00:31:37.291
your voice.

00:31:42.338 --> 00:31:43.380
My voice?

00:31:43.964 --> 00:31:47.009
I think your voice is cute, Cherry.

00:31:50.971 --> 00:31:52.890
<i>Cute…</i>

00:31:52.973 --> 00:31:54.600
<i>What does she mean?</i>

00:32:09.782 --> 00:32:12.201
LIGHTS IN THE SUMMER NIGHT
MAKE A FALSE START

00:32:18.040 --> 00:32:20.501
ARAKAWA MOVING CENTER

00:32:54.493 --> 00:32:56.620
Ouch…

00:32:59.164 --> 00:33:00.290
I'm home.

00:33:00.374 --> 00:33:02.001
Welcome back.

00:33:11.468 --> 00:33:13.137
Can I put this over there?

00:33:13.220 --> 00:33:15.347
What? Sure.

00:33:23.439 --> 00:33:25.691
Isn't it a bit early to start packing?

00:33:25.774 --> 00:33:28.110
We're not moving until next month.

00:33:28.694 --> 00:33:31.739
You'll be running around
last-minute anyway.

00:33:31.822 --> 00:33:34.116
It's better to start now.

00:33:34.199 --> 00:33:35.701
Well, I guess so.

00:33:36.827 --> 00:33:38.620
How's your back?

00:33:38.704 --> 00:33:40.456
It still hurts a bit.

00:33:40.539 --> 00:33:43.625
Don't push yourself.
I'll help with the chores.

00:33:43.709 --> 00:33:44.960
That'd be so helpful.

00:33:45.044 --> 00:33:46.962
Can you make breakfast?

00:33:47.046 --> 00:33:48.797
I told you I can't cook.

00:33:48.881 --> 00:33:50.758
You said you'd help, though.

00:33:50.841 --> 00:33:53.510
I meant with cleaning or shopping.

00:33:53.594 --> 00:33:55.471
That'd be a huge help, too.

00:33:55.554 --> 00:33:56.430
Huh?

00:33:57.139 --> 00:33:59.975
Yui, dinner's almost ready.

00:34:00.059 --> 00:34:00.934
Okay.

00:34:06.774 --> 00:34:07.691
I'm coming in.

00:34:07.775 --> 00:34:08.609
Okay.

00:34:35.177 --> 00:34:38.097
This <i>sajiki</i> dictionary
is easy to use, right?

00:34:38.597 --> 00:34:39.640
Yeah.

00:34:41.767 --> 00:34:44.269
It belongs to me, you know.

00:34:44.353 --> 00:34:45.771
Take good care of it.

00:34:45.854 --> 00:34:47.439
I know that.

00:34:50.651 --> 00:34:54.404
-Yui, aren't you upset with us moving?
-What?

00:34:54.488 --> 00:34:56.031
You keep packing.

00:34:58.659 --> 00:35:02.037
Everywhere is the same anyway,
as long as I have my phone.

00:35:04.123 --> 00:35:07.626
Thanks for doing
your mom's part-time job for her.

00:35:08.335 --> 00:35:09.211
It's fine.

00:35:09.294 --> 00:35:11.922
Try not to strain your back, okay?

00:35:12.005 --> 00:35:12.881
Okay.

00:35:14.007 --> 00:35:15.342
It's dinnertime.

00:35:15.425 --> 00:35:16.301
Sure.

00:35:25.519 --> 00:35:27.396
SUMMER BEGAN
WITH A BLINDING ENCOUNTER

00:35:29.815 --> 00:35:31.942
Oh, the haiku from earlier.

00:35:33.235 --> 00:35:34.069
#HAIKU

00:35:36.655 --> 00:35:37.781
Yuki.

00:35:39.283 --> 00:35:41.410
Don't use your phone during dinner.

00:35:41.493 --> 00:35:42.494
Okay.

00:35:45.956 --> 00:35:47.624
You too!

00:35:51.086 --> 00:35:52.129
Hey, Mom.

00:35:52.212 --> 00:35:53.255
Yeah?

00:35:53.338 --> 00:35:55.716
Stop liking my posts, seriously.

00:35:55.799 --> 00:35:58.218
What? Why?

00:35:58.302 --> 00:36:01.430
Aren't I the only one giving you likes?

00:36:10.314 --> 00:36:12.649
Don't use your phone during dinner.

00:36:12.733 --> 00:36:13.609
Just a second!

00:36:16.445 --> 00:36:17.529
Smile?

00:36:21.909 --> 00:36:22.868
What?

00:36:22.951 --> 00:36:25.704
You don't understand,
this is the least you can do.

00:36:25.787 --> 00:36:28.081
-Mari!
<i>-</i>Eat your food, you two!

00:36:28.165 --> 00:36:31.585
Does this mean she wants me to…

00:36:31.668 --> 00:36:33.045
follow her?

00:36:38.175 --> 00:36:39.801
Send him a reply.

00:36:39.885 --> 00:36:41.220
Come on, Juri.

00:36:41.303 --> 00:36:42.596
Oh, he followed you.

00:36:57.194 --> 00:36:59.112
SMILE: NOW FOLLOWING

00:37:11.458 --> 00:37:13.210
THE ONE WITH THE VOICE

00:37:13.293 --> 00:37:15.003
THAT'S HARD TO HEAR

00:37:15.087 --> 00:37:16.380
IS LOOKING FOR SUMMER

00:37:35.983 --> 00:37:36.817
CHERRY@HAIKU

00:37:36.900 --> 00:37:38.902
IN MY SEVENTEENTH JULY
I MET YOU

00:37:51.498 --> 00:37:54.918
SUBSCRIBE TO CHANNEL
128,463 FOLLOWERS

00:37:55.002 --> 00:37:56.003
HEY, SUNFLOWER

00:37:56.086 --> 00:37:58.922
I ASK MY DICTIONARY
THE DEFINITION OF "CUTE"

00:38:18.900 --> 00:38:20.819
SMILE

00:38:39.671 --> 00:38:41.423
SHADY SUMMER TEETH

00:38:41.506 --> 00:38:43.842
I JUST WANT TO KNOW WHY

00:38:49.431 --> 00:38:50.849
SHADY SUMMER LEAVES

00:38:50.932 --> 00:38:52.351
ALL I WANT TO KNOW IS WHY

00:39:27.677 --> 00:39:29.096
CHERRY@HAIKU

00:39:29.179 --> 00:39:33.475
WORDS BUBBLE UP
LIKE SODA POP

00:39:38.438 --> 00:39:40.232
JULY

00:39:40.315 --> 00:39:42.359
AUGUST

00:39:45.445 --> 00:39:46.780
THURSDAY, 1 AUGUST

00:39:47.697 --> 00:39:50.784
17 AUGUST: MOVING DAY

00:40:02.963 --> 00:40:05.382
"ODAYAMA DARUMA FOLK SONG:
DANCE PRACTICE VERSION"

00:40:18.061 --> 00:40:22.190
We're performing the Daruma Folk Song
at the mall's summer festival again.

00:40:22.774 --> 00:40:24.943
Everyone, let's give it our all!

00:40:25.026 --> 00:40:27.446
Okay!

00:40:28.029 --> 00:40:32.576
Don't you think this song is uncool?
I've always thought so.

00:40:32.659 --> 00:40:34.453
Yeah, you're right.

00:40:34.536 --> 00:40:37.372
It sounds rustic… Wait.

00:40:37.456 --> 00:40:38.498
Nami?

00:40:41.918 --> 00:40:45.672
Hearing this song
always brings back so many memories.

00:40:47.007 --> 00:40:49.217
What happened?

00:40:49.301 --> 00:40:52.554
I was so innocent…

00:40:57.058 --> 00:41:00.145
Fujiyama, you're riding
the shuttle car today.

00:41:00.228 --> 00:41:01.480
Uh-huh.

00:41:01.563 --> 00:41:03.064
Cherry. Smile.

00:41:03.148 --> 00:41:07.360
Akiko will bring the car out back,
so can you help Fujiyama.

00:41:07.444 --> 00:41:08.278
Okay.

00:41:19.789 --> 00:41:22.709
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

00:41:32.677 --> 00:41:35.305
"Fujiyama Records"?

00:41:37.432 --> 00:41:40.852
CLOSED

00:41:40.936 --> 00:41:45.357
OPEN

00:41:57.369 --> 00:42:00.372
Wow, what is all this?

00:42:24.854 --> 00:42:28.692
Are these… all records?

00:42:28.775 --> 00:42:30.151
You've never been here?

00:42:30.235 --> 00:42:31.945
I've never been inside.

00:42:40.287 --> 00:42:42.247
This record…

00:42:42.956 --> 00:42:43.790
is the one…

00:42:44.749 --> 00:42:46.668
I've listened to most.

00:42:49.045 --> 00:42:50.213
Over and over…

00:42:51.756 --> 00:42:52.882
Over and over…

00:42:58.888 --> 00:43:02.058
I want to listen to it one more time.

00:43:03.476 --> 00:43:05.562
If I could hear it one more time…

00:43:07.147 --> 00:43:08.481
I would remember.

00:43:09.524 --> 00:43:10.442
Remember what?

00:43:14.487 --> 00:43:16.281
I don't want to forget.

00:43:18.491 --> 00:43:20.327
I can't remember.

00:43:23.663 --> 00:43:25.373
I can't remember.

00:43:36.092 --> 00:43:37.177
Thank you.

00:43:40.680 --> 00:43:41.806
<i>"Yamazakura."</i>

00:43:42.849 --> 00:43:43.933
There's a hole.

00:43:48.688 --> 00:43:49.939
So cute.

00:43:53.276 --> 00:43:54.653
Something's inside.

00:44:00.075 --> 00:44:00.909
Look.

00:44:05.413 --> 00:44:10.293
<i>Farewell is something that's not said</i>
<i>Like the dance of cherry blossoms</i>

00:44:11.378 --> 00:44:12.212
Is it a haiku?

00:44:13.380 --> 00:44:14.923
<i>Farewell</i>

00:44:15.632 --> 00:44:17.384
<i>is something that's not said</i>

00:44:18.677 --> 00:44:20.929
<i>Like the dance of cherry blossoms</i>

00:44:29.104 --> 00:44:29.979
I'll look for it.

00:44:30.563 --> 00:44:31.606
Mr. Fujiyama.

00:44:32.273 --> 00:44:34.901
I'll look for the record, too.

00:44:36.736 --> 00:44:37.612
Me, too.

00:44:39.072 --> 00:44:40.407
I want him to hear it.

00:44:41.908 --> 00:44:47.163
I want him to remember
his precious memories.

00:44:52.752 --> 00:44:54.421
Are you okay? What's wrong?

00:44:54.504 --> 00:44:56.172
Mr. Fujiyama?

00:44:56.881 --> 00:44:58.299
Mr. Fujiyama!

00:44:58.842 --> 00:44:59.676
Dad!

00:45:00.844 --> 00:45:01.803
Dad!

00:45:18.319 --> 00:45:21.281
I wonder if Mr. Fujiyama is okay.

00:45:22.240 --> 00:45:23.116
Yeah.

00:45:25.034 --> 00:45:27.620
Maybe the record he's looking for…

00:45:28.747 --> 00:45:30.582
is inside that store.

00:45:32.167 --> 00:45:33.001
Yeah.

00:45:34.836 --> 00:45:39.090
But I wonder why
he was always searching around the mall.

00:45:42.343 --> 00:45:43.178
Um…

00:45:44.053 --> 00:45:45.722
-I'm--
-By the way…

00:45:47.974 --> 00:45:49.893
you haven't worn them lately.

00:45:57.484 --> 00:45:58.818
I don't need them.

00:45:58.902 --> 00:45:59.736
Huh?

00:46:00.445 --> 00:46:01.279
It's nothing.

00:46:16.461 --> 00:46:18.171
<i>Yamazakura…</i>

00:46:18.797 --> 00:46:22.217
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i> RECORD

00:46:36.272 --> 00:46:37.440
<i>About that record…</i>

00:46:38.024 --> 00:46:40.860
<i>The girl on the record had cute clothes,</i>

00:46:40.944 --> 00:46:42.612
<i>so I did an image search.</i>

00:46:44.322 --> 00:46:46.574
<i>The clothes were trendy</i>
<i>about 50 years ago.</i>

00:46:46.658 --> 00:46:48.618
<i>So the record's from back then.</i>

00:46:49.369 --> 00:46:51.496
Oh, this is about Mr. Fujiyama?

00:46:52.664 --> 00:46:55.834
Apparently he used to work here long ago.

00:46:55.917 --> 00:46:56.918
At the mall?

00:46:57.001 --> 00:46:58.545
No, no.

00:46:58.628 --> 00:47:02.632
Long ago,
this used to be a record pressing plant.

00:47:06.427 --> 00:47:09.013
<i>PHOTO ALBUM OF</i>
<i>NOUVELLE MALL'S HISTORY</i>

00:47:09.097 --> 00:47:10.348
ANNIVERSARY EXHIBIT

00:47:27.073 --> 00:47:29.075
These are Daruma Festival posters.

00:47:30.743 --> 00:47:33.288
They've had fireworks
ever since the first festival.

00:47:33.371 --> 00:47:34.330
Yeah.

00:47:35.039 --> 00:47:37.584
This year is the 56th festival…

00:47:37.667 --> 00:47:40.211
So it's continued for over 50 years.

00:47:42.672 --> 00:47:46.801
Someone who used to work
at the pressing factory?

00:47:47.802 --> 00:47:50.763
We hoped someone
would know about its past.

00:47:51.973 --> 00:47:53.975
Does anyone know someone like that?

00:47:57.478 --> 00:47:58.688
Oh, right.

00:47:58.771 --> 00:48:01.566
Why don't you try
Handoff on the third floor?

00:48:01.649 --> 00:48:05.570
They have old records there, don't they?

00:48:05.653 --> 00:48:09.574
We don't have any records
called <i>Yamazakura.</i>

00:48:09.657 --> 00:48:11.618
I see.

00:48:11.701 --> 00:48:17.248
Oh, but I think that record
might be a picture disc!

00:48:17.874 --> 00:48:18.958
A picture disc?

00:48:19.792 --> 00:48:21.753
It looks like this.

00:48:21.836 --> 00:48:23.588
What's this? It's so cute!

00:48:23.671 --> 00:48:25.173
Right?

00:48:25.256 --> 00:48:27.926
It's a limited-edition Hikarun record!

00:48:28.676 --> 00:48:33.514
Picture disc jackets often have a hole
so that you can see inside.

00:48:34.599 --> 00:48:37.977
The one in your photo
has a hole in the middle, too.

00:48:38.061 --> 00:48:39.562
I see.

00:48:39.646 --> 00:48:41.314
You're amazing, Japan.

00:48:41.397 --> 00:48:42.523
Oh, it's nothing.

00:48:42.607 --> 00:48:44.400
What? Is this a treasure hunt?

00:48:45.193 --> 00:48:46.611
Yeah, kinda like that.

00:48:46.694 --> 00:48:48.947
What? I wanna join too!

00:48:50.073 --> 00:48:52.867
<i>Apparently this record is a picture disc.</i>

00:48:54.535 --> 00:48:56.579
<i>Does anyone recognize it?</i>

00:48:57.914 --> 00:49:00.208
<i>-Nope, no idea.</i>
<i>-Never seen it before.</i>

00:49:00.291 --> 00:49:02.502
<i>-Any clues?</i>
<i>-I'll ask my grandpa!</i>

00:49:02.585 --> 00:49:06.214
<i>I guess nobody knows, huh?</i>

00:49:10.843 --> 00:49:12.762
<i>The radio tower up Mt. Umafuse?</i>

00:49:14.639 --> 00:49:18.351
"Isn't this the radio tower
up Mt. Umafuse?"

00:49:18.434 --> 00:49:21.104
"On the south side of Oda City."

00:49:21.604 --> 00:49:23.940
"The <i>yamazakura</i> blossoms there
are famous."

00:49:47.922 --> 00:49:50.842
YOSHIDA WARD, ODA CITY
MT. UMAFUSE ARTIFACTS

00:50:03.646 --> 00:50:04.480
Look here.

00:50:07.400 --> 00:50:10.069
SINGER-SONGWRITER FROM ODA CITY

00:50:10.153 --> 00:50:12.321
SAKURA FUJIYAMA

00:50:18.953 --> 00:50:22.623
"A singer-songwriter from Oda City."

00:50:22.707 --> 00:50:25.168
"Sakura Fujiyama, 22 years old."

00:50:26.169 --> 00:50:28.671
"Her latest record is <i>Yamazakura</i>."

00:50:29.964 --> 00:50:32.050
Her surname is…

00:50:32.133 --> 00:50:33.092
Yeah.

00:50:34.093 --> 00:50:35.261
It's Fujiyama.

00:50:37.346 --> 00:50:38.598
Mom.

00:50:40.683 --> 00:50:44.771
That means this person
is Mr. Fujiyama's…

00:50:44.854 --> 00:50:46.606
-wife?
-Yes.

00:50:48.066 --> 00:50:51.986
So Mom really was a musician, huh?

00:50:53.571 --> 00:50:55.865
Um, where is she now?

00:50:56.699 --> 00:51:01.120
I heard she got sick and passed away
soon after giving birth to me.

00:51:01.204 --> 00:51:04.874
I was really young,
so I don't remember anything.

00:51:08.044 --> 00:51:10.046
My father opened this shop

00:51:10.129 --> 00:51:13.382
so that he could sell my mother's records.

00:51:13.466 --> 00:51:15.384
I see.

00:51:17.553 --> 00:51:20.890
We're actually shutting down this weekend.

00:51:22.975 --> 00:51:25.978
It's grown old
and no one will take over.

00:51:26.938 --> 00:51:29.607
Yasuyuki's packing it up right now.

00:51:32.777 --> 00:51:34.987
Darn, this is tiring.

00:51:36.489 --> 00:51:37.615
Any progress?

00:51:38.199 --> 00:51:39.951
I'm working on it.

00:51:40.034 --> 00:51:41.452
Oh, it's you guys.

00:51:41.536 --> 00:51:43.121
Why are you two here?

00:51:44.038 --> 00:51:45.289
Just stopping by.

00:51:45.373 --> 00:51:46.582
Stopping by?

00:51:55.591 --> 00:51:57.176
I think Mr. Fujiyama…

00:51:59.011 --> 00:52:01.180
wants to hear Sakura's voice.

00:52:02.515 --> 00:52:04.934
That's why he's looking so hard for it.

00:52:09.814 --> 00:52:10.648
Um…

00:52:11.941 --> 00:52:12.775
I…

00:52:16.154 --> 00:52:19.615
Can I help pack up the records, too?

00:52:19.699 --> 00:52:21.576
-Huh?
-What?

00:52:21.659 --> 00:52:26.164
The record that Mr. Fujiyama
is looking for might be in here.

00:52:26.247 --> 00:52:27.081
Hey, hold on.

00:52:27.165 --> 00:52:28.291
Me, too!

00:52:28.374 --> 00:52:29.667
What?

00:52:35.256 --> 00:52:36.507
To be honest…

00:52:39.510 --> 00:52:41.137
I've looked, too.

00:52:43.890 --> 00:52:45.892
But I couldn't find it.

00:52:49.228 --> 00:52:50.771
If we all look together…

00:52:51.772 --> 00:52:53.357
maybe we'll find it.

00:52:57.069 --> 00:52:59.155
Let's get Beaver and Japan to help, too.

00:52:59.238 --> 00:53:00.198
Okay!

00:53:00.281 --> 00:53:02.325
Hey, wait a second.

00:53:02.408 --> 00:53:05.494
What is this record
that my grandpa is looking for?

00:53:06.245 --> 00:53:08.122
Don't you want to hear it too?

00:53:08.706 --> 00:53:10.249
It's your grandma's voice.

00:53:11.209 --> 00:53:14.587
I WOULDN'T HAVE COME ALONE

00:53:14.670 --> 00:53:16.130
SHOOTING GRASS ARROWS

00:53:16.214 --> 00:53:19.133
AUGUST 14

00:53:22.220 --> 00:53:24.138
OPEN

00:53:47.411 --> 00:53:50.081
Geez, it's so hot.

00:53:50.164 --> 00:53:50.998
You're right.

00:53:51.082 --> 00:53:52.708
I'm seriously gonna melt.

00:53:52.792 --> 00:53:54.085
Get used to it.

00:53:54.168 --> 00:53:56.212
The air conditioner is broken.

00:53:56.295 --> 00:53:58.714
The fan will have to do.

00:54:03.678 --> 00:54:04.762
You could take it off.

00:54:06.597 --> 00:54:08.599
Well, it's, um…

00:54:08.683 --> 00:54:10.476
It's really dusty in here.

00:54:12.061 --> 00:54:15.189
Hey everyone, I made some <i>sōmen</i> noodles.

00:54:15.273 --> 00:54:16.857
It's time for food!

00:54:23.114 --> 00:54:25.283
Hey, where's Smile?

00:54:25.366 --> 00:54:27.827
She said she's on a diet.

00:54:43.050 --> 00:54:46.637
Wow, I feel so refreshed!

00:54:55.354 --> 00:54:57.690
The record's not here.

00:54:58.607 --> 00:55:00.568
We still have another half to go.

00:55:07.158 --> 00:55:09.160
<i>HAIKU: AUGUST</i>

00:55:43.361 --> 00:55:45.029
<i>HAIKU: MARCH</i>
<i>KIGO FOR SPRING</i>

00:55:45.112 --> 00:55:49.033
THE TRUE MEANINGS OF THESE <i>KIGO:</i>
"WHITEBAIT" AND "YAMAZAKURA"

00:55:59.001 --> 00:56:00.044
"Yamazakura"…

00:56:01.337 --> 00:56:02.671
HAIKU TRIVIA

00:56:02.755 --> 00:56:06.050
"Yamazakura leaves grow
before its cherry blossoms,

00:56:06.133 --> 00:56:10.429
so people with buck teeth
are referred to as 'Yamazakura.'"

00:56:28.739 --> 00:56:32.284
I wonder how Sakura felt.

00:56:40.042 --> 00:56:42.002
Cherry posted a new haiku.

00:56:49.260 --> 00:56:50.511
<i>Yamazakura</i>

00:56:51.011 --> 00:56:55.516
<i>I like the leaves that you've hidden</i>

00:57:00.604 --> 00:57:05.359
YAMAZAKURA
I LIKE THE LEAVES THAT YOU'VE HIDDEN

00:57:29.633 --> 00:57:32.553
AUGUST 15

00:58:23.312 --> 00:58:25.356
So it's not here after all.

00:58:36.492 --> 00:58:39.119
Thanks, Cherry.

00:58:39.203 --> 00:58:40.496
You too, Smile.

00:58:58.180 --> 00:58:59.932
Yasuyuki?

00:59:00.015 --> 00:59:02.977
Can you pack up the fridge
and the fan, too?

00:59:04.645 --> 00:59:07.106
-I'll do it tomorrow.
-Thanks.

00:59:25.291 --> 00:59:26.417
It's not here.

00:59:34.091 --> 00:59:35.384
Darn it.

00:59:44.977 --> 00:59:46.437
What is it?

00:59:53.068 --> 00:59:53.902
Oh!

00:59:56.989 --> 00:59:57.990
Here it is.

00:59:58.073 --> 00:59:59.950
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

01:00:00.909 --> 01:00:02.494
-We found it.
-Yeah.

01:00:03.037 --> 01:00:04.330
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

01:00:04.413 --> 01:00:06.415
Dad!

01:00:09.293 --> 01:00:12.212
<i>YAMAZAKURA</i>

01:00:17.926 --> 01:00:18.969
Sakura.

01:00:20.346 --> 01:00:21.972
I'll get Japan to play it.

01:00:25.142 --> 01:00:26.143
Thanks.

01:00:28.854 --> 01:00:30.773
Where's the speaker cable?

01:00:30.856 --> 01:00:32.733
I think it's on the veranda.

01:00:49.249 --> 01:00:50.084
Hey.

01:00:50.918 --> 01:00:51.794
Look at this.

01:00:55.255 --> 01:00:56.382
Fireworks.

01:00:57.174 --> 01:00:58.592
Isn't it cute?

01:00:58.676 --> 01:01:00.386
Cute?

01:01:00.469 --> 01:01:01.303
Yeah.

01:01:06.225 --> 01:01:07.559
The Daruma Festival…

01:01:11.021 --> 01:01:12.106
is in two days.

01:01:17.069 --> 01:01:18.570
Yeah.

01:01:22.199 --> 01:01:23.075
Let's…

01:01:28.080 --> 01:01:30.416
see the fireworks together.

01:01:42.970 --> 01:01:43.804
Um…

01:01:49.977 --> 01:01:52.312
-I'm--
-Cherry! Bring the cable!

01:01:52.938 --> 01:01:54.523
Hurry up already!

01:01:55.983 --> 01:01:57.109
Um…

01:01:59.319 --> 01:02:00.404
Let's go.

01:02:22.468 --> 01:02:24.470
It's kinda warped.

01:02:29.016 --> 01:02:30.100
I wonder…

01:02:31.143 --> 01:02:33.187
if this will play properly.

01:02:45.449 --> 01:02:46.533
No way.

01:02:48.911 --> 01:02:49.745
Smile.

01:02:56.126 --> 01:02:57.211
Where's the record?

01:02:58.003 --> 01:02:59.296
Is something wrong?

01:03:16.271 --> 01:03:19.691
AUGUST 16

01:03:21.652 --> 01:03:22.486
Yui.

01:03:23.278 --> 01:03:26.782
I'm going to visit
Hidamari in the evening.

01:03:26.865 --> 01:03:28.450
Tell the manager for me.

01:03:29.576 --> 01:03:30.494
Sure.

01:03:49.930 --> 01:03:53.934
Our performance is tomorrow at seven
on the rooftop stage, okay?

01:03:54.017 --> 01:03:55.477
Okay.

01:03:57.646 --> 01:03:58.480
Cherry.

01:04:02.568 --> 01:04:06.196
Can you come with me after this?

01:04:07.614 --> 01:04:13.745
I want to apologize
to Mr. Fujiyama one more time.

01:04:13.829 --> 01:04:14.663
NOTICE

01:04:14.746 --> 01:04:16.707
MR. FUJIYAMA IS NOT PRESENT TODAY

01:04:16.790 --> 01:04:17.791
Of course.

01:04:17.875 --> 01:04:19.251
Thanks.

01:04:22.921 --> 01:04:23.755
Um…

01:04:27.676 --> 01:04:28.719
Actually, I…

01:04:28.802 --> 01:04:29.970
Hello.

01:04:30.470 --> 01:04:31.889
Oh, Maria!

01:04:32.472 --> 01:04:34.349
It's been so long.

01:04:34.433 --> 01:04:36.393
Long time, no see.

01:04:36.476 --> 01:04:39.354
How's your back?
Are you okay now?

01:04:39.438 --> 01:04:41.440
Yes, thanks for asking.

01:04:43.358 --> 01:04:44.985
Who is she?

01:04:45.068 --> 01:04:45.986
She's…

01:04:47.154 --> 01:04:48.238
my mom.

01:04:49.740 --> 01:04:53.744
Everyone, thank you
for watching after my son.

01:04:55.495 --> 01:05:00.083
Sakura, thank you so much
for all your help until now.

01:05:00.167 --> 01:05:03.086
You did a great job
stepping in for Maria.

01:05:03.170 --> 01:05:07.007
But it's a shame we can't dance
the Daruma Folk Song together.

01:05:22.481 --> 01:05:26.318
I'm sorry for not telling you
that I'm moving.

01:05:30.864 --> 01:05:32.282
When did you find out?

01:05:34.868 --> 01:05:37.329
When summer break started.

01:05:45.420 --> 01:05:47.255
-What about the fireworks?
-Huh?

01:05:48.674 --> 01:05:50.384
You said we'd go together.

01:05:55.263 --> 01:05:56.098
I'm sorry.

01:06:06.650 --> 01:06:07.651
I see.

01:06:12.781 --> 01:06:13.615
Then…

01:06:14.950 --> 01:06:15.993
take care.

01:06:50.944 --> 01:06:55.866
A THUNDEROUS ROAR
WORDS EXIST FOR THE SAKE OF EXPRESSION

01:06:55.949 --> 01:06:59.745
OPEN

01:06:59.828 --> 01:07:04.624
CLOSED

01:07:16.094 --> 01:07:17.429
Mr. Fujiyama.

01:09:40.989 --> 01:09:46.411
THE GOLDFISH BOWL
HAS CRACKED AND IS FLOWING

01:10:08.350 --> 01:10:11.269
Now, I would like to announce the start

01:10:11.353 --> 01:10:15.106
of the 56th Odayama Daruma Festival!

01:10:31.748 --> 01:10:33.250
You're finally awake.

01:10:37.754 --> 01:10:38.588
Here.

01:10:44.552 --> 01:10:45.387
Thanks.

01:10:54.104 --> 01:10:54.938
Hey!

01:10:55.772 --> 01:10:57.148
Come here!

01:11:22.215 --> 01:11:25.010
ARAKAWA MOVING CENTER

01:11:30.098 --> 01:11:31.266
Coming!

01:11:31.349 --> 01:11:34.060
We're from the Arakawa Moving Center!

01:11:34.144 --> 01:11:36.062
Thank you for coming.

01:11:36.146 --> 01:11:37.731
Thank you!

01:12:15.435 --> 01:12:16.311
I'm…

01:12:16.895 --> 01:12:17.896
really sorry.

01:12:21.775 --> 01:12:23.777
Oh, it's a record.

01:12:26.529 --> 01:12:27.364
Thanks.

01:12:28.823 --> 01:12:30.867
Wow, amazing.

01:12:31.868 --> 01:12:32.786
That's…

01:12:33.370 --> 01:12:34.204
a record?

01:12:35.789 --> 01:12:39.209
I feel like I've seen this before.

01:12:41.378 --> 01:12:44.923
Everyone, it's almost time,
so let's go to the stage.

01:12:45.006 --> 01:12:46.508
Look!

01:13:19.958 --> 01:13:20.917
A record?

01:13:21.835 --> 01:13:22.794
Amazing!

01:13:23.628 --> 01:13:28.133
If only Cherry weren't moving today.

01:13:28.216 --> 01:13:30.927
We could've all heard it together.

01:13:51.865 --> 01:13:53.908
Um, can I ask you all a favor?

01:14:00.123 --> 01:14:04.377
APARTMENTS WITH FRESH IVY
WE'RE IN NUMBER 305

01:14:30.153 --> 01:14:32.322
SMILE HAS STARTED A LIVESTREAM

01:14:44.334 --> 01:14:45.168
And now,

01:14:45.251 --> 01:14:50.215
here is a dance by everyone
from Day Service Hidamari!

01:14:51.049 --> 01:14:54.219
Please enjoy
this Odayama Daruma Folk Song!

01:15:17.575 --> 01:15:19.953
Huh? That's not the right song.

01:15:33.841 --> 01:15:39.430
<i>♪ Remember back to those days ♪</i>

01:15:40.473 --> 01:15:44.227
<i>♪ When we lived in a dream ♪</i>

01:15:46.854 --> 01:15:52.193
<i>♪ And to our meeting of chance ♪</i>

01:15:53.861 --> 01:15:57.699
<i>♪ It was a miracle from this world ♪</i>

01:16:00.493 --> 01:16:02.161
<i>♪ On that day ♪</i>

01:16:02.996 --> 01:16:05.415
<i>♪ At the concert venue ♪</i>

01:16:05.957 --> 01:16:09.794
<i>♪ We fell in love ♪</i>

01:16:10.461 --> 01:16:14.215
<i>♪ As if struck by lightning ♪</i>

01:16:17.218 --> 01:16:22.807
<i>♪ The key that opens</i>
<i>the gate to my heart ♪</i>

01:16:23.850 --> 01:16:28.479
<i>♪ The one and only key ♪</i>

01:16:30.315 --> 01:16:34.944
<i>♪ Wings that guide us to freedom ♪</i>

01:16:35.945 --> 01:16:39.115
<i>♪ The dream we once let go of ♪</i>

01:16:39.741 --> 01:16:44.287
<i>♪ Becomes a rainbow bridge ♪</i>

01:16:57.342 --> 01:16:58.801
This song…

01:16:59.552 --> 01:17:01.012
Mr. Fujiyama's record?

01:17:31.751 --> 01:17:35.421
